[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/asasher/asher-skills/pulls/201","id":4231235782,"node_id":"PR_kwDOSiAors78M4jG","html_url":"https://github.com/asasher/asher-skills/pull/201","diff_url":"https://github.com/asasher/asher-skills/pull/201.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/asasher/asher-skills/pull/201.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/asasher/asher-skills/issues/201","number":201,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Simplify the development skill family, refresh staffing, and add CLIProxyAPI images","user":{"login":"asasher","id":4597866,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1OTc4NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4597866?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/asasher","html_url":"https://github.com/asasher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asasher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asasher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asasher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asasher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asasher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asasher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asasher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asasher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/asasher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The software development family now follows one ticket through groom, shape, build, merge, and retro. Groom reads all open issues, preserves native dependencies during consolidation, and routes clear work directly to ready. Milestones group testing batches; approved spec splits define integration branches. Shaping and builds use secondary worktrees, recover pushed branches, and preserve ownership and checkpoints across machines.\n\nBuild owners implement and fix inline, obtain independent code review and risk-appropriate verification, publish inspected evidence outside Git, and open ordinary PRs for human selection. Reports identify the tested integration tree. Merge checks current approval and shaping holds, honors configured branch protection and checks merge freshness without requiring protection, and preserves active or unique work during cleanup. Retro saves a pending batch of local session versions and presents project issue drafts for user selection.\n\nInstructions remove redundant negations, routine command recipes, duplicate policy, and arbitrary diagnosis and diagram rules. Label setup uses a compact table. The worktree helper skill and Relay are retired. Standalone worktree guards, prelaunch reservations, bounded review, isolated headless browser verification, and human approval boundaries remain. Staffing assigns Astra to planning and execution, Fable 5.1 to taste and frontend design, and Terra to bounded collection and capture.\n\nFixes #208: the bundled image adapter selects configured CLIProxyAPI, then native Codex, then direct OpenAI API with an available Platform key and explicit authorization. Native results must belong to the launched session; generation and sprite extraction use the same chroma key. Artifact publication rejects occupied or symbolic targets. T3 retains worker identity through ambiguous responses or credential-cleanup failures, and auth/naming waits are bounded.\n\nThe visual family guide, manual review order, and adversarial report describe the final contracts and remaining eval plan. The mobile Markdown reader exposes all 385 package files across the unchanged 36-skill install set and preserves internal links. The original reviewer reports remain as historical evidence.\n\nValidation:\n\n- 72 offline helper tests pass: 6 artifact-branch, 32 dispatch/naming, and 34 image-backend tests. New failure regressions were demonstrated red before their fixes.\n- Sprite acceptance covers 14 criteria plus bounds sanity; the versioning dry run passes.\n- Three fresh independent reviews closed additional authority, symbolic-ref, response-decoding, and embedded-motion findings. A headless browser check confirms two motion figures operate independently with one shared controller.\n- Metadata and dependencies pass for all 46 authored skills; the 36-skill install closure and runtime package boundaries pass. Formatting and diff checks pass.\n- Mobile/desktop report checks pass; all 385 reader sources load and 2,034 local links and anchors resolve. Earlier live CLIProxyAPI smoke returned an inspected image and correctly reported its dimension mismatch.\n\nBehavior will be assessed through actual work in integrations-v2 after installation and reconciliation, as selected by the user. Synthetic agent fixtures are retired as a rollout gate. Live native-format compatibility, T3 failure recovery, repository merge behavior, and Linux browser isolation remain capability-specific observations to establish where used.\n\n`backlog build` drains the initial frontier: ready-for-agent tickets with no open blockers, admitted under global ownership and capacity rules. A selected approved spec or milestone advances through successive waves, preserving branch targets and human merge selection. Worker deadlines bound waits; queue and tracker checkpoints support resume. Review-ready PRs remain distinct from confirmed delivery completion.\n","created_at":"2026-08-07T19:51:33Z","updated_at":"2026-09-13T07:51:09Z","closed_at":"2026-09-13T07:51:09Z","merged_at":"2026-09-13T07:51:09Z","merge_commit_sha":"d828cbf38f7d855fa391e69e366c79693f33579a","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/asasher/asher-skills/pulls/201/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/asasher/asher-skills/pulls/201/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/asasher/asher-skills/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/rep